248
00:23:19.340 --> 00:23:40.380
<v Noah Labhart>So that all makes sense to me. So you mentioned in chapter eight that compensation can be a distraction. And I fully agree there. What core mistakes do scaling startups make with compensation that turn it from a non-issue into an energy sapping problem that erodes retention? So focusing on the wrong thing, but what mistakes do those startups make?

